WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.780
Fight, crash through, and face the challenge!

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.000
These are our hard knock days.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.830
Can't quench our thirst with a peaceful, everyday life.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.340
Here we go - don't ever run away!

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.450
Let's go on living as the mighty winds take us!

7
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.870
We've still got so far to go.

8
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.390
Gotta keep going through the hard knock days.

9
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.610
Let's do it again, yes, baby. How many times

10
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.110
do I have to stand back up to make my dream come true?

11
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.730
Feels like the strength of my resolve

12
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.200
is put to the test everyday.

13
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.700
Hey, let's go!

14
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.450
I don't want to make excuses and settle for being mediocre.

15
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.900
Hey, let's go!

16
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.670
We leapt into a crazy, lawless world.

17
00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.110
As I struggled for a foothold, reality caught me off guard.

18
00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:59.370
Even if it beats me, hits me, knocks me down again,

19
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.220
Oh!

20
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.500
Only when we get back on our feet and look forward,

21
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.450
will we have the last laugh, be the winners!

22
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.120
We gotta go down this glory road, till we reach our goal!

23
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.630
Fight, shake it off, act strong!

24
00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.630
These are our hard knock days.

25
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.680
There's no such thing as a safe choice.

26
00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.890
Here we go - we'll always be the strongest!

27
00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:27.270
Let's keep moving - never mind the consequences.

28
00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.860
Let's put our wishes all together,

29
00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:34.650
and keep on going through the hard knock days.

30
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.260
<b>Prostration</b>

31
00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.140
Room!

32
00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:29.900
Chambres!

33
00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.100
Oh! He's been saved!

34
00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.020
Lucy!

35
00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:48.750
<b>Underground Trading
Port Dock</b>

36
00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.650
Look! Nobody's up there now!

37
00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:09.920
How did it go?!

38
00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.210
What just happened?

39
00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.120
Tell us, Gatz!

40
00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.140
Gatz-san!

41
00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.260
You can't yell anymore!

42
00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:22.940
Don't push yourself!

43
00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.820
You fools!

44
00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.580
What kind of announcer am I if I can't announce the winner and the loser?

45
00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.300
Look, you two!

46
00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.540
Look to the sky, Dressrosa!

47
00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.000
Which is fading?

48
00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:19.900
The bird cage?

49
00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.980
Or Doflamingo's domination?

50
00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.500
The factory just...

51
00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.480
The bird cage is...

52
00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.180
The strings...

53
00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.880
Are gone!

54
00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.870
I can see the sky! The sky!

55
00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.420
The sky!

56
00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:59.360
I-Is the scenery outside of the cage...

57
00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:02.840
a town that's been carved into pieces?

58
00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.760
Or is it...

59
00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:10.920
a land where no one will manipulate us anymore - a land of freedom?

60
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.200
The bird cage's gone!

61
00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:21.300
That means...

62
00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.620
The "Great Defense of Dressrosa"!

63
00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:32.090
The two thousand pirates of the Donquixote Family...

64
00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.240
versus

65
00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:38.480
the fated warriors, here by coincidence!

66
00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.400
And the duel between their leaders!

67
00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:01.580
Royal Warlord of the Sea, Donquixote Doflamingo...

68
00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.850
versus

69
00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:06.760
the gladiator, Lucy!

70
00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:13.440
Dah winnah...

71
00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.220
What?

72
00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.240
Dah winnah...

73
00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.290
What's he saying?

74
00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.610
It's "the winner"!

75
00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.680
Dah winnah ish...

76
00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.140
You can do it, Gatz-san!

77
00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.770
Dah winnah...

78
00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.850
Stay with us, Gatz!

79
00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.580
Who's there?!

80
00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:44.280
Don't shout. Don't call for anyone.

81
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.400
I am Donquixote Doflamingo.

82
00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:54.180
I am the rightful king of this kingdom.

83
00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:57.790
The king has returned!

84
00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:00.080
Is it something we did?

85
00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.830
There is no excuse for this.

86
00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:06.520
The country is done for!

87
00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.820
This was Doflamingo's trap!

88
00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:14.120
Dah winnah...

89
00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.790
Get a grip already!

90
00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.540
Speak clearly!

91
00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.440
Listen, Rebecca.

92
00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.060
Don't cry yet.

93
00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.070
I won't let the soldier die.

94
00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:33.440
Make sure you stay safe.

95
00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:37.580
I'm gonna beat the crap outta Doflamingo!

96
00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.840
Lucy...

97
00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:48.330
The winner is...

98
00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:54.780
...Lucy!

99
00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.820
Lucy!

100
00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.660
Thank you, Lucy!

101
00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:07.860
This is the best!

102
00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.010
He did it!

103
00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.920
Super!

104
00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.730
Luffyland!

105
00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:15.500
Luffy!

106
00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.150
Robiland!

107
00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:26.440
Luffy!

108
00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:29.290
He finally did it!

109
00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.910
Well done, my boy!

110
00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.610
Truly incredible!

111
00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:45.270
Expect nothing less of Luffy-dono!

112
00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:52.060
Princess!

113
00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.960
I'm so glad!

114
00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.000
Fraland!

115
00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:01.020
All of you did great, too!

116
00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:02.620
You're hurting us!

117
00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:09.930
We toys were once human!

118
00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.520
Captain!

119
00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.740
They will fight alongside us.

120
00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.710
They are the dwarfs of the Tontatta Kingdom.

121
00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:21.760
Are you really sure about leaving her?

122
00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.750
She was crying!

123
00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:27.440
Even toys have something they want to protect!

124
00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:32.000
Although these tin eyes of mine cannot shed tears.

125
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:38.440
That's why the captain has been fighting on his own for ten years.

126
00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:55.420
What have you done to this country and the king, pirate?!

127
00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:59.860
The king set the city ablaze.
Didn't you see him?

128
00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.960
His Majesty would never do such a thing!

129
00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:08.620
This battle is to restore the honor of King Riku who was dethroned in shame ten years ago,

130
00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:12.440
and to regain our freedom!

131
00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:28.940
Soldier-san!

132
00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:30.930
I will not let you take...

133
00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:33.340
another member of my family from me!

134
00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:53.260
A country in ruins needn't necessarily be unhappy.

135
00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.600
On this day, amid piles of rubble, the people of this very country...

136
00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.800
cried out in joy.

137
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.320
Hooray!

138
00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.720
Doflamingo was taken down!

139
00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.990
We're free from now on!

140
00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:15.820
Mom! Dad!

141
00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:16.680
Thank God!

142
00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:23.080
Gatz-san!

143
00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:25.820
Yeah, he did it!

144
00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.550
So aren't you gonna finish me off?

145
00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:41.640
Don't need to.

146
00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.780
Seems like it's all over.

147
00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:52.680
You brothers are too soft!

148
00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:07.620
After losing to our captain at Banaro Island,

149
00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:11.040
Ace had something to say
before he was handed over to the Navy.

150
00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:12.560
Wanna hear it?

151
00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:19.250
<b>Underground Port</b>

152
00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:19.200
Hey, hurry up!
The duel between Straw Hat and Doflamingo is over!

153
00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:21.370
The Navy'll be here soon!

154
00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:22.620
We know!

155
00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:24.470
You call the chief yet?

156
00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:25.960
We're trying!

157
00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.660
He's not picking up.

158
00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:31.860
He only answers when he feels like it.

159
00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.120
You'll get a kick outta hearin' it!

160
00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:50.500
He realized he was gonna be executed, so he said...

161
00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.180
Don't tell my brother.

162
00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:05.240
Man, what an idiot!

163
00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:08.420
He had no idea how much he was worth!

164
00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:15.830
If Fire Fist Ace was captured by the Navy,
the news would spread all over the world!

165
00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:19.800
The Navy would make 120% use of his pathetic life-

166
00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:27.680
That's quite enough.

167
00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.580
Stop talking.

168
00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:38.380
How he felt when he passed away...

169
00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:40.180
<b>Fire Fist Ace Dies</b>

170
00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:47.460
I've thought about it non-stop
since that day, every single night.

171
00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:52.790
You don't have to tell me. I fully understand!

172
00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:02.060
Then let it sink in, fool!

173
00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.850
As for that Devil Fruit you have...

174
00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:10.200
If I can't steal it here, it'll damage
my reputation as a hunter of Devil Fruit users.

175
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.900
You're not getting away from me, Flame Fruit!

176
00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.260
You're regretting it, aren't you?!

177
00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:20.340
Even though you had the title and the power,

178
00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:23.220
you still didn't try to save your brother!

179
00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:26.620
You weren't there at all, were you?!

180
00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:29.260
Were you taking a nap or something?

181
00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:33.390
You weren't there when he needed you most.

182
00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:36.320
And you call yourselves brothers!

183
00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.700
I'm done regretting it!

184
00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.000
Fire Fist!

185
00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.540
Dammit!

186
00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:17.550
I've made peace with it,
but Ace is saying he can't forgive you.

187
00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.150
Oh! Hello, Sabo-kun?

188
00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.140
Where in the world are you?!

189
00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:32.750
I saw Burgess going after Luffy-kun earlier,

190
00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:37.020
so I frantically tried to contact you, but you weren't answering at all!

191
00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:39.290
That so? I wasn't paying attention.

192
00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:40.190
You weren't what?!

193
00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:42.420
Don't worry, I took care of it already.

194
00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.030
That aside, Koala, have you found the list?

195
00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:48.590
For crying out... Yes, I found it!

196
00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.270
Then just call the ship and-

197
00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:51.260
I called it!

198
00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:53.830
Well, let's meet up with Hack underground then.

199
00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:56.340
I'm with Hack and everyone else underground!

200
00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.830
Why did he hang up?! That selfish jerk!

201
00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:11.160
Stop taking it out on me, Koala-san!

202
00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:23.380
There he is!

203
00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:28.530
The Donquixote Family!

204
00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:45.960
Their eight commanders and...

205
00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:55.180
...three top commanders are all accounted for!

206
00:18:58.510 --> 00:18:59.530
Watch out!

207
00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:03.060
Most of the commanders are Devil Fruit users!

208
00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:08.680
Secure them with Sea Stone!

209
00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:09.580
Yes, sir!

210
00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.060
Just stay here with me.

211
00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:20.400
Yes.

212
00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.060
Whoa! Wh-What're you doing?!

213
00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:25.370
You said, "Stay here with me"!

214
00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.380
So we'll be together forever!

215
00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:27.380
Get off of me!

216
00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.360
Have we contacted Navy HQ yet?

217
00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:40.420
Well, actually...

218
00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:44.340
Isshou-san said, "Don't file a report yet."

219
00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:54.420
Vice Admiral Maynard!
The Surveillance Snail is ready!

220
00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:58.280
Alright, I'll do the talking.

221
00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:04.530
Take another Surveillance Snail
and follow Isshou-san, per orders!

222
00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:05.200
Yes, sir!

223
00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:16.790
<b>Applenine - A Neighboring Country</b>

224
00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.780
This is Applenine Island, a country near Dressrosa.

225
00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:21.820
What the heck?

226
00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:23.160
What's wrong?

227
00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.860
I heard there'll be a broadcast from Dressrosa!

228
00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:28.740
Will it be a speech from King Doflamingo?

229
00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:30.640
Scary, isn't it?

230
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.640
This is Dressrosa...

231
00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:37.020
<b>Another Neighboring Country</b>

232
00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:44.200
We are broadcasting to the three neighboring island countries within range of the Surveillance Snail.

233
00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:47.180
<b>Yet Another Neighboring Country</b>

234
00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:58.850
I am Navy HQ Vice Admiral Maynard!

235
00:20:58.850 --> 00:20:59.820
The Navy?

236
00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:02.020
This is Dressrosa.

237
00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:07.800
We are broadcasting to the three neighboring island countries within range of the Surveillance Snail.

238
00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:08.870
But why?

239
00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:11.600
I want you to take a look at these images!

240
00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.700
What's up with the piles of rubble?

241
00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:21.280
What you're seeing is
the current state of Dressrosa!

242
00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:23.820
What does he mean?

243
00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:26.450
I ask you to keep calm as I tell you...

244
00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:32.960
all the details of what the Warlord,
Donquixote Doflamingo, did today in this very country!

245
00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:38.060
Isshou-san, I'll do as you asked.

246
00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:45.810
We're begging you, Your Majesty!

247
00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:50.980
So many of us citizens were turned into toys and couldn't speak out!

248
00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:54.800
No! Please... stop this.

249
00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:04.560
Even if the misunderstanding about me has cleared up,
I cannot return as your king.

250
00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:08.300
No! You are this country's true king!

251
00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.510
That's right!

252
00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:11.540
We're sick and tired of violence!

253
00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:12.580
Your Majesty!

254
00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:16.780
What if everyone in the kingdom shared your values?

255
00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.840
Wait.

256
00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:31.060
The Riku Family's position falls apart when faced with turmoil.

257
00:22:31.540 --> 00:22:34.280
This event has proven that.

258
00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:38.860
We don't care if we fall to ruin!

259
00:22:39.800 --> 00:22:43.260
We'd gladly fall to ruin if there were
any hope for peace together with you!

260
00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:47.110
We want you to renounce war, as our pacifist king!

261
00:22:47.110 --> 00:22:48.310
That's right!

262
00:22:48.310 --> 00:22:52.180
Even if it causes our country to fall, we're fine with that!

263
00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:58.600
We don't mind being poor!
Just make Dressrosa a peaceful country again!

264
00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:00.010
Your Majesty!

265
00:23:00.010 --> 00:23:02.220
Your Majesty, we're begging you!

266
00:23:11.880 --> 00:23:14.260
As a fighting king, their words grate my ears!

267
00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:17.100
Elizabello!

268
00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:22.340
Your Majesty! You must return to the palace at once!

269
00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:26.400
Kings from neighboring countries keep calling us!

270
00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:28.000
What did you say?

271
00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:33.910
I had to tell them right away...

272
00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:38.540
that King Riku is coming back.
They were all overjoyed to hear that!

273
00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:40.360
The King of Prodence!

274
00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:46.120
It's barely been a decade.
How could you age so much?

275
00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:52.840
Where is the man who would stare down the world to avoid a war?

276
00:23:55.440 --> 00:23:57.580
Your people are waiting for you.

277
00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:02.160
Come home...

278
00:24:02.880 --> 00:24:05.480
Miracle King, Riku Dold!

279
00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:10.680
He is right, King Riku!

280
00:24:27.080 --> 00:24:30.250
All this trouble that Doflamingo caused...

281
00:24:30.250 --> 00:24:35.080
I would rather you not take responsibility for it.

282
00:24:35.920 --> 00:24:43.740
That vicious pirate was approved as king of a country
under the Seven Warlords system,

283
00:24:43.740 --> 00:24:47.780
and thus permitted to reign over this island by none other than...

284
00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:51.460
the World Government!

285
00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:58.160
To all who inhabit this country...

286
00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:01.320
and to all members of its royal family...

287
00:25:11.740 --> 00:25:14.540
On behalf of the Government,

288
00:25:14.540 --> 00:25:19.560
I most humbly apologize!

289
00:25:46.260 --> 00:25:50.580
We most deeply regret what has been done!

290
00:25:52.880 --> 00:25:54.480
What are you...

291
00:26:05.640 --> 00:26:08.600
The Navy admiral has prostrated himself?

292
00:26:08.940 --> 00:26:09.960
You're kidding me...

293
00:26:13.860 --> 00:26:15.840
The Government controls the Navy!

294
00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:19.480
And one of the Navy admirals,
the greatest of their military might...

295
00:26:19.480 --> 00:26:22.970
is bowing before King Riku and his nation in apology!

296
00:26:22.970 --> 00:26:25.310
What the heck is going on in Dressrosa?

297
00:26:24.890 --> 00:26:29.290
<b>Law - Straw Hat Pirate Alliance</b>

298
00:26:25.310 --> 00:26:29.400
That pirate alliance took down
the Celestial Yaksha, Doflamingo?

299
00:26:30.240 --> 00:26:32.540
Take pictures! Put them in print already!

300
00:26:33.500 --> 00:26:35.600
This is completely unheard of!

301
00:26:38.360 --> 00:26:43.880
The false glory of the mighty country, Dressrosa, and the truth behind it.

302
00:26:44.700 --> 00:26:51.060
The downfall of the world's greatest
underground broker, Doflamingo.

303
00:26:51.920 --> 00:26:57.100
And the prostration of Navy HQ Admiral Fujitora.

304
00:26:57.700 --> 00:27:00.700
The major incidents that were confined within the cage...

305
00:27:05.340 --> 00:27:10.860
have just been released to the entire world.

306
00:27:39.340 --> 00:27:41.670
An admiral from
Navy HQ has prostrated himself?!

307
00:27:41.670 --> 00:27:43.880
The Surveillance Snail is running, too!

308
00:27:51.160 --> 00:27:53.780
Th-That's a Navy admiral, isn't it?

309
00:27:55.300 --> 00:27:56.590
Wh-What happened?

310
00:27:56.590 --> 00:27:58.880
Something's going on in Dressrosa!

311
00:28:01.660 --> 00:28:04.500
Raise your head, Fujitora.

312
00:28:08.340 --> 00:28:12.460
Fujitora, aren't you worried about the world seeing this?

313
00:28:17.510 --> 00:28:18.720
You couldn't possibly...

314
00:28:19.510 --> 00:28:21.180
Could it be...

315
00:28:22.320 --> 00:28:25.500
that you stayed away from Doflamingo so you could enact this?

316
00:28:29.700 --> 00:28:30.970
Fujitora!

317
00:28:30.970 --> 00:28:33.640
The world must know the truth!

318
00:28:34.340 --> 00:28:39.860
I left all the fighting to them.
I made a wager on them.

319
00:28:40.340 --> 00:28:44.020
We are the ones who allowed the Warlords to do as they please.

320
00:28:44.020 --> 00:28:47.640
So who are we to point our swords at them,

321
00:28:47.640 --> 00:28:51.780
and yet preach about justice without bearing shame?

322
00:28:58.240 --> 00:29:08.520
This country earned its victory at the hands of pirates, warriors, and its citizens!

323
00:29:09.070 --> 00:29:12.280
Our long, hard battle is at last over.

324
00:29:12.660 --> 00:29:13.920
I am truly...

325
00:29:16.820 --> 00:29:18.660
I am truly grateful for your hard work.

326
00:29:20.180 --> 00:29:23.660
Little Army of King Riku, Special Anti-Doflamingo Forces!

327
00:29:23.660 --> 00:29:26.140
Yes, Commander!

328
00:29:26.880 --> 00:29:28.740
As of today, you are all...

329
00:29:32.680 --> 00:29:33.760
...dismissed!

330
00:29:35.340 --> 00:29:40.600
Commander!

331
00:29:41.170 --> 00:29:41.940
Tank!

332
00:29:42.760 --> 00:29:44.940
The Navy still has their position to consider.

333
00:29:44.940 --> 00:29:48.860
Hide the pirates and warriors
who fought for us in the palace.

334
00:29:49.340 --> 00:29:52.980
Take those without shelter there as well.
I hate to ask, but can I count on you?

335
00:29:52.980 --> 00:29:55.440
Of course, it would be my pleasure, Your Majesty!

336
00:30:04.660 --> 00:30:12.150
<b>The Red Line</b>

337
00:30:12.670 --> 00:30:16.310
<b>Holy Land, Mariejois</b>

338
00:30:14.700 --> 00:30:15.800
So...

339
00:30:16.540 --> 00:30:20.140
Reporting Doflamingo's resignation, and then revealing it as false...

340
00:30:20.600 --> 00:30:25.100
Was this all by order of those people above you?

341
00:30:24.520 --> 00:30:30.160
<b>World Government Supreme Authority
The Five Elder Stars</b>

342
00:30:30.980 --> 00:30:36.870
<b>Navy Headquarters Fleet Admiral
Sakazuki (Akainu)</b>

343
00:30:31.440 --> 00:30:34.160
Why should the world be deceived

344
00:30:34.160 --> 00:30:36.740
for the sake of someone like Doflamingo?!

345
00:30:37.320 --> 00:30:42.400
If something like this ever happens again,
it'll bring shame on me as fleet admiral!

346
00:30:42.960 --> 00:30:45.080
Don't ever do that again, under any circumstances!

347
00:30:45.880 --> 00:30:49.270
Don't give us any of your cheek, Sakazuki.

348
00:30:49.270 --> 00:30:52.040
Your honor is completely inconsequential.

349
00:30:52.820 --> 00:30:56.540
The Navy is merely the public face of the Government.

350
00:30:56.920 --> 00:31:00.520
We left this case entirely up to Cipher Pol.

351
00:31:00.920 --> 00:31:03.100
Hmph! Cipher Pol, huh?

352
00:31:04.440 --> 00:31:06.020
So simply put,

353
00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:09.640
they've gone over your heads.

354
00:31:10.020 --> 00:31:12.190
Those damn puppets of the Celestial Dragons!

355
00:31:12.190 --> 00:31:14.340
Watch your mouth, Sakazuki!

356
00:31:14.340 --> 00:31:16.460
And what of Kuzan's actions?

357
00:31:18.120 --> 00:31:22.880
I can hardly believe a powerful man like him
sides with Blackbeard now.

358
00:31:24.020 --> 00:31:26.660
That is sure to bring dishonor to the Navy!

359
00:31:26.660 --> 00:31:30.280
That idiot resigned from the Navy!

360
00:31:30.280 --> 00:31:34.420
Where he is and what he's doing is not our responsibility!

361
00:31:34.980 --> 00:31:37.000
Five Elder Stars! Fleet Admiral Sakazuki!

362
00:31:43.520 --> 00:31:44.900
Reporting in!

363
00:31:44.900 --> 00:31:52.000
The Warlord, Donquixote Doflamingo, and his family
were defeated by the Law - Straw Hat Pirate Alliance.

364
00:31:52.340 --> 00:31:55.940
And Dressrosa has been destroyed.
There's nothing left of it!

365
00:31:56.920 --> 00:31:58.160
What'd you say?!

366
00:32:02.160 --> 00:32:03.240
Again...

367
00:32:03.240 --> 00:32:04.800
...with that brat?

368
00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:10.460
And there's one more thing...

369
00:32:25.130 --> 00:32:29.620
<b>Countries Across the New World</b>

370
00:32:25.470 --> 00:32:30.980
The video and story that were sent to Dressrosa's neighbors spread from one island to the next.

371
00:32:31.980 --> 00:32:34.200
Extra! Extra!

372
00:32:34.480 --> 00:32:38.510
The news spread like wildfire
throughout the world, with dire repercussions.

373
00:32:35.500 --> 00:32:37.430
Doflamingo Falls!!

374
00:32:38.940 --> 00:32:40.720
Joker was defeated!

375
00:32:41.660 --> 00:32:45.000
Your Majesty!
We have no other way to acquire weapons!

376
00:32:47.490 --> 00:32:49.480
Announce our surrender.

377
00:32:55.260 --> 00:32:57.780
The war is over!

378
00:32:59.760 --> 00:33:03.480
We've already paid! We had a deal!

379
00:33:03.480 --> 00:33:05.280
That bastard, Joker!

380
00:33:05.820 --> 00:33:08.190
I know they still have weapons in Dressrosa!

381
00:33:08.190 --> 00:33:10.730
Don't! There's still a Navy admiral over there!

382
00:33:10.730 --> 00:33:13.190
Our deal for the Devil Fruits!

383
00:33:13.190 --> 00:33:15.890
What'll happen to the Smiles deal now?!

384
00:33:15.890 --> 00:33:17.960
If only these fools weren't there!

385
00:33:24.500 --> 00:33:28.570
Come now, Tsuru-chan!
You didn't need to tag along with us!

386
00:33:28.570 --> 00:33:31.120
I ought to be saying that, Inspector General!

387
00:33:31.600 --> 00:33:35.680
Well, they're the pirate group that you've been chasing after all this time, aren't they?

388
00:33:35.680 --> 00:33:37.240
Yes, under your orders.

389
00:33:37.740 --> 00:33:39.320
Want some rice crackers?

390
00:33:39.200 --> 00:33:41.300
<b>In a Certain Town</b>

391
00:33:41.640 --> 00:33:45.320
How's this? This is today's special mixed pizza.

392
00:33:46.320 --> 00:33:47.250
Huh? Thief!

393
00:33:47.250 --> 00:33:48.950
Hey, old lady! Stop!

394
00:33:50.160 --> 00:33:51.980
Crap, where did she go?

395
00:33:56.660 --> 00:33:59.510
Tsk, just a little girl. Old lady, where'd you go?!

396
00:33:59.510 --> 00:34:02.900
Oh, they took down Doflamingo.

397
00:34:03.280 --> 00:34:06.520
Not bad.
Makes me happy to be from the same generation.

398
00:34:07.500 --> 00:34:11.370
<b>From South Blue - Captain of the Bonney Pirates
"The Glutton" Jewelry Bonney</b>

399
00:34:11.480 --> 00:34:15.600
<b>In a certain sky</b>

400
00:34:19.520 --> 00:34:21.300
High Priest Urouge!

401
00:34:22.880 --> 00:34:24.480
High Priest Urouge!

402
00:34:27.620 --> 00:34:30.980
Th-There's somebody here! High Priest!

403
00:34:31.380 --> 00:34:37.500
<b>From the Sky Islands - Captain of the Fallen Monk Pirates
"Mad Monk" Urouge</b>

404
00:34:31.980 --> 00:34:35.450
Nonsense! We're on a Sky Island.

405
00:34:35.450 --> 00:34:38.300
It's an abandoned and isolated cloud island, at that.

406
00:34:38.640 --> 00:34:40.220
Nobody but us could possibly-

407
00:34:51.150 --> 00:34:56.170
<b>In a certain sea</b>

408
00:34:52.780 --> 00:34:56.200
Whoa, whoa, not bad, that pirate alliance.

409
00:34:56.840 --> 00:35:00.080
Looks like my fellow pirates ain't doing too shabby.

410
00:34:56.990 --> 00:35:03.470
<b>From West Blue - Captain of the Fire Tank Pirates
Capone "Gang" Bege</b>

411
00:35:00.620 --> 00:35:03.760
Capture Caesar at any cost, boys!

412
00:35:03.760 --> 00:35:05.580
Yes, Father!

413
00:35:05.910 --> 00:35:09.310
<b>The Kid Pirates' Hideout</b>

414
00:35:09.840 --> 00:35:12.360
They made their move before we knew it.

415
00:35:12.680 --> 00:35:14.790
It's a huge victory!

416
00:35:14.790 --> 00:35:17.890
Doflamingo is connected to Kaidou behind the scenes, for sure.

417
00:35:17.890 --> 00:35:20.160
Well, that's gonna make Kaidou pretty mad, yeah?

418
00:35:20.090 --> 00:35:24.120
<b>From South Blue - Captain of the Kid Pirates
Eustass "Captain" Kid</b>

419
00:35:21.020 --> 00:35:24.700
If they planned this, their target must be...

420
00:35:24.300 --> 00:35:28.370
<b>From North Blue - Captain of the Hawkins Pirates
"The Mage" Basil Hawkins</b>

421
00:35:26.910 --> 00:35:28.720
...one of the Four Emperors, as we thought.

422
00:35:28.520 --> 00:35:32.750
<b>From the Grand Line (Longarm Tribe) - Captain of the On-Air Pirates
"Roaring Tide" Scratchmen Apoo</b>

423
00:35:30.840 --> 00:35:32.900
"Beast King" Kaidou, eh?

424
00:35:32.900 --> 00:35:37.300
<b>From South Blue - Kid Pirates Combatant
"Soldier of Slaughter" Killer</b>

425
00:35:34.910 --> 00:35:37.860
Good thing our target isn't theirs.

426
00:35:38.400 --> 00:35:41.320
We won't have to fight each other
and waste our military might.

427
00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:47.620
Our target is one of the other Four Emperors,
"Red Hair" Shanks!

428
00:35:48.940 --> 00:35:52.890
And now we shift attention to Drake,
who once provoked a battle in Kaidou's territory...

429
00:35:52.590 --> 00:35:54.900
<b>A Certain Island</b>

430
00:35:53.340 --> 00:35:56.420
Your father was killed? By Doflamingo?

431
00:36:04.100 --> 00:36:06.900
That was a long time ago. I bear no grudge.

432
00:36:04.850 --> 00:36:10.870
<b>From North Blue - Captain of the Drake Pirates
"Red Flag" X-Drake</b>

433
00:36:06.900 --> 00:36:09.620
What gives? That's pretty heartless of you.

434
00:36:09.620 --> 00:36:11.140
Hey, give us a hand here!

435
00:36:11.540 --> 00:36:15.720
This is an emergency!
If we don't let him know right away, he'll snap!

436
00:36:16.560 --> 00:36:19.550
Kaidou-sama! Where are you?

437
00:36:19.550 --> 00:36:22.360
That idiot Joker screwed up big time!

438
00:36:22.360 --> 00:36:25.000
We won't be receiving Smiles anymore!

439
00:36:27.200 --> 00:36:29.380
Don't play dumb with me, Isshou!

440
00:36:29.300 --> 00:36:31.690
<b>Dressrosa</b>

441
00:36:32.120 --> 00:36:37.240
You know full well the gravity of
a Navy admiral admitting to oversight!

442
00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:40.800
Why didn't you report to HQ first?!

443
00:36:42.740 --> 00:36:48.820
Had I reported in, surely you would have changed
the details of the report yet again, would you not?

444
00:36:49.920 --> 00:36:51.560
What did you just say?!

445
00:36:56.840 --> 00:37:00.600
I also feel the Seven Warlord system must end.

446
00:37:05.100 --> 00:37:10.440
Two years ago, I was there when Crocodile showed his true nature.

447
00:37:11.760 --> 00:37:14.280
The Navy couldn't do anything!

448
00:37:19.180 --> 00:37:21.630
If it weren't for the Straw Hats,

449
00:37:21.630 --> 00:37:26.560
Alabasta would be another country
governed by a pirate, just like Dressrosa.

450
00:37:27.100 --> 00:37:31.580
Yet the Government reported that it was the Navy's doing!

451
00:37:33.480 --> 00:37:36.620
If only I held higher rank then!

452
00:37:49.840 --> 00:37:54.480
I can't believe Fujitora really did it.

453
00:37:54.800 --> 00:37:58.500
It reminds me of the frustration I felt
at Alabasta Kingdom two years ago.

454
00:37:59.860 --> 00:38:03.560
The Straw Hats' triumph was covered up then.

455
00:38:05.580 --> 00:38:07.980
It's like he paid them back for us.

456
00:38:08.500 --> 00:38:12.440
Even if I held the same rank as him,
I couldn't have pulled that off.

457
00:38:12.980 --> 00:38:14.560
I could feast on this feeling for days.

458
00:38:15.460 --> 00:38:18.100
Oh, we have muffins! How about some coffee?

459
00:38:18.100 --> 00:38:19.930
That didn't mean I wanted to eat, you idiot!

460
00:38:21.440 --> 00:38:23.290
Hey lady, I'm hungry!

461
00:38:23.290 --> 00:38:24.620
We're hungry too!

462
00:38:25.100 --> 00:38:27.480
We have muffins! How about some coffee?

463
00:38:27.480 --> 00:38:29.800
You can't give kids coffee!

464
00:38:29.800 --> 00:38:31.230
I want a muffin!

465
00:38:31.230 --> 00:38:32.900
Are we at Megapants' yet?

466
00:38:32.900 --> 00:38:34.060
That's "Vegapunk".

467
00:38:34.500 --> 00:38:38.220
It'll be a few more days until we reach Dr. Vegapunk's lab.

468
00:38:40.080 --> 00:38:43.180
How lovely!
Captain-chan's sweet to the kids!

469
00:38:43.180 --> 00:38:44.970
I wish I were a kid!

470
00:38:44.970 --> 00:38:48.110
Hey, you bunch!
There's still tons of work to do!

471
00:38:48.110 --> 00:38:49.290
Aye aye, ma'am!

472
00:38:49.290 --> 00:38:51.420
Scold me more, Captain-chan!

473
00:39:09.080 --> 00:39:11.740
Cover-ups happen all the time!

474
00:39:12.080 --> 00:39:16.240
I would rather not be a hero forged upon lies.

475
00:39:16.560 --> 00:39:24.930
It was our employer, the World Government,
that hired pirates to maintain balance in the world.

476
00:39:24.930 --> 00:39:28.420
This is a matter of the Navy's credibility and dignity!

477
00:39:28.480 --> 00:39:31.380
I-Isshou-san, y-you're talking to...

478
00:39:32.660 --> 00:39:37.380
Your selfish actions dishonor the very name of justice!

479
00:39:37.380 --> 00:39:41.960
If you value your justice so damn much,
then keep a close eye on it!

480
00:39:41.960 --> 00:39:47.640
If we lose credibility just for admitting fault,
we haven't any in the first place!

481
00:39:55.030 --> 00:39:58.560
Then you clean up after yourself, Fujitora!

482
00:39:59.740 --> 00:40:04.600
Straw Hat and Law... Until you bring me their heads,

483
00:40:05.000 --> 00:40:09.180
you are hereby barred from setting foot within any Navy base in the world!

484
00:40:10.680 --> 00:40:14.680
Good, that's exactly what I wanted to hear.

485
00:40:16.260 --> 00:40:18.340
Meat...
